WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.950
AJA HAMMERLY: Did
you know that you

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.199
can create an instance group
template from a container

00:00:03.199 --> 00:00:03.730
image?

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.150
I'll show you how.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.770
Start at the Compute section
on the cloud console.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.048
Click Instance Groups,
Create Instance Group.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:13.968
Name your group.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.280
Select a location.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.710
And under Instance Definition,
choose Create a New Container

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.380
Instance Template.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.261
Name your template.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.310
Select a machine type.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.360
And then put in the path
to your container image.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.540
My container image is on
Google Cloud Registry.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.700
You can select a boot disk
type, set up any ports,

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.980
and turn on HTTP and HTTPS
traffic if you need to.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.610
Click Save and Continue.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.690
Choose the number of instances.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.770
And you can set up auto
healing if you'd like.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.910
Now click Create.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.560
Once your group is created, you
can click Instance Templates

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.875
and find your template there.

00:00:56.875 --> 00:01:00.160
I hope you get a
chance to try this out.

